The TLS library set up before connecting (lynx-patches/0001's HTSSLFree): lynx made the TCP connection first and
set up OpenSSL (the first time: its configuration, providers and ciphers, the kept sessions) only then, inside
HTSSLConnect. On the Tab5's emulated Pentium that takes ~1.5 s, and some servers close a connection whose request
hasn't come in 5 s (lynx.invisible-island.net, lynx's own start page, never opened there).

--- a/WWW/Library/Implementation/HTTP.c
+++ b/WWW/Library/Implementation/HTTP.c
@@ -557,9 +557,16 @@
     line_kept_clean = NULL;
 
 #ifdef USE_SSL
-    if (!StrNCmp(url, "https", 5))
+    if (!StrNCmp(url, "https", 5)) {
+	/*
+	 * The TLS library's setup (the first time: its configuration, the
+	 * ciphers, the kept sessions) before connecting, not between the
+	 * connection and the request: on a slow CPU it takes seconds, and some
+	 * servers close a connection whose request hasn't come in 5.
+	 */
+	HTSSLFree(HTGetSSLHandle());
 	status = HTDoConnect(url, "HTTPS", HTTPS_PORT, &s);
-    else
+    } else
 	status = HTDoConnect(url, "HTTP", HTTP_PORT, &s);
 #else
     if (!StrNCmp(url, "https", 5)) {
